      "message": "\u003e libprotobuf-mutator depends on protobuf which depends on the c++ standard library which depends on cstdlib as implmented in clang. It is possible to write a fuzzing target without these, but it costs the time required to right a good model with a mutator.\n\nAck, makes sense. You could technically separate the protobuf handling from the actual fuzzing and linking the former against the cstdlib part, but the latter only against EC. That\u0027d be pretty awkward though, and you\u0027d need custom structs to pass data. So while I\u0027m still not too excited about the stdlib hiding approach (as you have certainly realized by now), I don\u0027t have a better suggestion at this point so I\u0027ll shut up now :)\n\n\u003e Another example is openssl which I believe also depends on cstdlib, though I could probably remove this dependency since we don\u0027t really need to do the encryption for real in the fuzzer.\n\nI guess you could technically keep the dcrypto functions undefined in the ec part, and then link them in with the stdlib-dependent part. Anyhow, I\u0027m already convinced that what you have is the best practical trade-off, so not relevant :)",
